  arm A: the checker's own mr_proof_stages (rectform third in the radcan family)
  arm B: MR_PROOF_STAGES with rectform LAST, after rat-radcan
Entries (08-stage-order-entries.py, from test/corpus_class<N>.geteqr.out = master b62d6d7, old checker):
  unverified -- all 1,551 `unverified` entries;
  control    -- 1,000 `verified` entries, proportional per class, floor 25, seed 20260929.

== findings
- The order changes NO verdict: 0 class transitions in either set. Wall per arm is the same
  (unverified 13.0 / 13.2 min, control 6.2 / 5.7 min).
- Moving rectform last does not remove its cost: 351 -> 356 rectform stage timeouts on the
  unverified set. Those entries are unprovable, so every stage runs in any order.
- rectform is the ONLY stage that proves 9 of the 2,551 entries (arm B, where it runs last): 1.2.1.2
  e1376, 3.5 e169/e210, 4.1.10 e33, 4.2.7 e80/e83, 4.6.11 e38, 6.2.7 e70/e73. 5 more that it
  closed in arm A are closed by logarc once rectform runs after it.
- Heap: 7 entries reach the heap guard in both arms (1.2.1.2 e724, 1.2.1.4 e369/e373, 4.5.1.2
  e713-e716). In arm A, rectform's garbage also stops the stages after it (trigexpand, demoivre).
- rat-radcan is the only stage that proves 1 entry (5.1.4a e439, arm B, where only rectform follows it).
- Control: 1,000 / 1,000 still PASS; 135 move verified -> expected (the self-diff is not proved, the
  expected-diff is: by design). 34 (3.4 %) pass on the numeric check only (21 of them after a
  stage timeout); by section 1.2 10, 1.1 9, 4.5 5, 4.2 3, 4.1 2, 2.3/4.3/7.3/7.5/7.6 1.
- The unverified set under this branch: 546 of 1,551 now PASS (356 verified, 190 expected); 36
  numeric mismatches remain (master's triage had ~190).

